<title>UK: Brent sells at Dec -50 cents.</title>
<headline>Brent sells at Dec -50 cents.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>A cargo of Brent loading November 8-10 was sold at December -50 cents to a big trading house, traders said.</p>
<p>This was 10 cents below Thursday's levels and the seller anticipated more price falls.</p>
<p>&quot;I sold at this level because I expect to buy cheaper,&quot; the trader said.</p>
<p>--Kate Dourian, London newsroom +44 171 542 4088</p>
